{"seq":27,"slug":"queueing-theory","title":"排队论","stage":"DONE","category":"mathematics-statistics","chapterCount":4,"docCount":12,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/mathematics-statistics/queueing-theory","rating":{"composite":4.04,"verdict":"stable","groups":{"quality":3.6,"coverage":3.5,"positioning":5,"strategic":4.33},"weights":{"quality":0.3,"coverage":0.25,"positioning":0.2,"strategic":0.25},"profile":null},"introHtml":"<h1 id=\"排队论\">排队论</h1><p>排在咖啡店收银台后面、刷新一个迟迟不返回的网页、看着工厂里半成品堆在某台机器前——这些日常的「等待」背后，是同一套数学。排队论研究的核心只有一句话：当随机到达的请求遇上有限的服务能力，等待如何产生、有多长、队伍排多长。它不预测某一个顾客何时被服务，而是刻画大量随机事件叠加后的<strong>统计规律</strong>，并据此回答工程上最实际的问题——要多少服务台、利用率压到多少、延迟的尾部有多糟。</p>\n<p>本 hub 沿四条主线层层递进。第一条「基础」铺设语言：到达过程、服务时间、排队规则这三件套构成一切模型的原料，Kendall 记号把它们压缩成 <code>A/B/c/K/N/D</code> 的紧凑标签，而 Little 定律给出一条不依赖任何分布假设的铁律 <span class=\"math-inline\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>λ</mi><mi>W</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">L=\\lambda W</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">L</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">λW</span></span></span></span></span>。第二条「经典模型」把基础落到可解的具体系统：M/M/1 用生灭过程给出最干净的闭式解，M/M/c 推广到多服务台并引出 Erlang C 排班公式，M/G/1 用 Pollaczek–Khinchine 公式揭示「服务时间方差」才是延迟的隐形杀手。第三条「排队网络」把单个队列连成系统：Jackson 网络的乘积形式定理让复杂网络奇迹般地解耦，开/闭网络与 MVA 算法处理有限客户数的闭式循环，瓶颈分析则用渐近界回答「加机器加在哪里」。第四条「实践」把理论交给工程师：容量规划给出利用率与冗余的取舍法则，性能工程把这套语言对接到软件系统的尾延迟与通用可扩展性定律 USL，仿真则在解析模型失效时兜底。</p>\n<p><strong>本 hub 与兄弟 hub 的分工边界</strong>：排队论是<a href=\"../stochastic-processes/\">随机过程</a>的一个应用分支——后者负责泊松过程、连续时间 Markov 链、生灭过程这些<strong>通用机理</strong>，本 hub 只在用到时一句话引入并链接过去，专注于「队列」这一特定结构的建模与工程结论。指数分布、方差、条件期望这些概率工具属于<a href=\"../probability-statistics/\">概率统计</a>，本 hub 默认你已掌握、不再展开。涉及「最优服务台数」「成本最小化」的求解则与<a href=\"../optimization-theory/\">最优化理论</a>接壤，本 hub 给出目标函数、把求解交给那边。</p>\n<p><strong>推荐学习路径</strong>：若你是软件/系统工程师，按 <code>基础 → M/M/1 → M/M/c → 瓶颈分析 → 性能工程</code> 走最短路，直奔容量与延迟的工程结论；若你是运筹/数学背景的读者，按章节顺序通读，重点在网络一章的乘积形式与 MVA；若只想要一个能立刻用的工具，先读 Little 定律与 M/M/1，再跳到容量规划。</p>\n<p><strong>前置知识</strong>：指数分布与泊松分布的基本性质、期望与方差、几何级数求和；网络一章额外需要一点线性方程组与 Markov 链平稳分布的概念，可随时回到随机过程 hub 补齐。读完本 hub，你应当能拿到一个真实系统的到达率与服务率，估出平均延迟、判断它会不会因负载升高而雪崩、并算出该加几台机器。</p>\n","chapters":[{"seq":1,"slug":"foundations","title":"基础","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/mathematics-statistics/queueing-theory/foundations","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"queueing-elements","title":"排队系统要素","url":"/l-doc-books/h/mathematics-statistics/queueing-theory/foundations/queueing-elements"},{"seq":2,"slug":"kendall-notation","title":"Kendall 记号","url":"/l-doc-books/h/mathematics-statistics/queueing-theory/foundations/kendall-notation"},{"seq":3,"slug":"littles-law","title":"Little 定律","url":"/l-doc-books/h/mathematics-statistics/queueing-theory/foundations/littles-law"}]},{"seq":2,"slug":"models","title":"经典模型","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/mathematics-statistics/queueing-theory/models","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"mm1-queue","title":"M/M/1 队列","url":"/l-doc-books/h/mathematics-statistics/queueing-theory/models/mm1-queue"},{"seq":2,"slug":"mmc-multiserver","title":"M/M/c 多服务台","url":"/l-doc-books/h/mathematics-statistics/queueing-theory/models/mmc-multiserver"},{"seq":3,"slug":"mg1-general-service","title":"M/G/1 与一般服务","url":"/l-doc-books/h/mathematics-statistics/queueing-theory/models/mg1-general-service"}]},{"seq":3,"slug":"networks","title":"排队网络","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/mathematics-statistics/queueing-theory/networks","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"jackson-networks","title":"Jackson 网络","url":"/l-doc-books/h/mathematics-statistics/queueing-theory/networks/jackson-networks"},{"seq":2,"slug":"open-closed-networks","title":"开闭排队网络","url":"/l-doc-books/h/mathematics-statistics/queueing-theory/networks/open-closed-networks"},{"seq":3,"slug":"bottleneck-analysis","title":"瓶颈分析","url":"/l-doc-books/h/mathematics-statistics/queueing-theory/networks/bottleneck-analysis"}]},{"seq":4,"slug":"practice","title":"实践","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/mathematics-statistics/queueing-theory/practice","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"capacity-planning","title":"容量规划","url":"/l-doc-books/h/mathematics-statistics/queueing-theory/practice/capacity-planning"},{"seq":2,"slug":"performance-engineering-queueing","title":"性能工程应用","url":"/l-doc-books/h/mathematics-statistics/queueing-theory/practice/performance-engineering-queueing"},{"seq":3,"slug":"queueing-simulation","title":"排队仿真","url":"/l-doc-books/h/mathematics-statistics/queueing-theory/practice/queueing-simulation"}]}]}